// Hole shapes for Speed Carpentry. Each entry is
//   [shape, piece combinations that fill it, weight]
// where the shape lists rows of 1 (hole) and 0 (wood), each row ended by a 2, and each
// combination is the letters of the pieces that fill it. When speed carp asks for a
// particular piece, the desktop version uses these lists filtered to combinations
// containing it (see holesWith in carp.ts); two-piece holes for "x" had one extra hole
// added so there are always enough to choose from.
export type HoleEntry = readonly [shape: string, combinations: readonly string[], weight: number];

